    "role": "tool",
    "content": [
      {
        "cache_prompt": false,
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/skills/tsci_built_in_elements/capacitor.md:\n     1\t# <capacitor />\n     2\t\n     3\t## Overview[\u200b](#overview \"Direct link to Overview\")\n     4\t\n     5\tA `<capacitor />` stores electrical energy in an electric field. Capacitors are commonly used for filtering, energy storage, and timing circuits. Unlike resistors, capacitors can be polarized (like electrolytic capacitors) or non-polarized (like ceramic capacitors).\n     6\t\n     7\tA capacitor element has two pins. Polarized capacitors must be placed with correct orientation to avoid damage.\n     8\t\n     9\tWhen specifying a capacitor, you'll need to provide a footprint string (like `0402` or `0805`) and capacitance value. Popular capacitor types and sizes can be found at [jlcsearch](https://jlcsearch.tscircuit.com/capacitors/list).\n    10\t\n    11\t```\n    12\texport default () => ( <board width=\"10mm\" height=\"10mm\">  <capacitor    name=\"C2\"    footprint=\"axial_p5mm\"    capacitance=\"10\u03bcF\"    polarized  /> </board>)\n    13\t```\n    14\t\n    15\t## Pins[\u200b](#pins \"Direct link to Pins\")\n    16\t| Pin # | Aliases (Polarized) | Description |\n    17\t| --- | --- | --- |\n    18\t| pin1 | pos, anode, left | The positive terminal (required for polarized capacitors) |\n    19\t| pin2 | neg, cathode, right | The negative terminal (must be connected properly for polarized caps) |\n    20\t\n    21\t## Specifications[\u200b](#specifications \"Direct link to Specifications\")\n    22\t\n    23\tCapacitors can be configured with these key properties:\n    24\t\n    25\t-   **capacitance** - The capacitance value specified as a string e.g. `\"100nF\"` or `\"2.2\u03bcF\"`\n    26\t-   **voltageRating** - Maximum voltage the capacitor can handle e.g. `\"25V\"`\n    27\t-   **tolerance** - Capacitance tolerance percentage e.g. `\"\u00b110%\"`\n    28\t-   **temperatureCoefficient** - Temperature stability specification e.g. `\"X7R\"`\n    29\t-   **equivalentSeriesResistance** - ESR value for critical applications e.g. `\"0.5\u03a9\"`\n    30\t\n    31\t## Schematic Orientation\n    32\t\n    33\tPolarized capacitors can display their positive and negative pins in different orientations. Use the `schOrientation` property to control the symbol orientation instead of manually setting `schRotation`.\n    34\t\n    35\tValid orientation values are:\n    36\t\n    37\t-   `horizontal`\n    38\t-   `vertical`\n    39\t-   `pos_left`\n    40\t-   `pos_right`\n    41\t-   `pos_top`\n    42\t-   `pos_bottom`\n    43\t-   `neg_left`\n    44\t-   `neg_right`\n    45\t-   `neg_top`\n    46\t-   `neg_bottom`\n    47\t\n    48\t```\n    49\t<capacitor  name=\"C1\"  capacitance=\"1uF\"  polarized  schOrientation=\"pos_left\"  schX={0}  schY={0}  connections={{ pos: \"net.POS\", neg: \"net.NEG\" }}/>```\n    50\t```\n",
        "enable_truncation": true
      }
    ],
