    "content": [
      {
        "cache_prompt": false,
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/skills/tsci_built_in_elements/battery.md:\n     1\t# <battery />\n     2\t\n     3\t## Overview[\u7ab6\u72a0(#overview \"Direct link to Overview\")\n     4\t\n     5\tA `<battery />` is a power source that provides electrical energy through electrochemical reactions. Batteries are essential components that supply power to electronic circuits and devices. They have a positive and negative terminal and must be connected with correct polarity.\n     6\t\n     7\tA battery element has two pins and is polarized, meaning it has a positive terminal (cathode) and a negative terminal (anode). The voltage and capacity of the battery determine how much power it can provide and for how long.\n     8\t\n     9\tWhen specifying a battery, you'll need to provide the voltage rating and optionally the capacity. Common battery types include AA, AAA, 9V, coin cells, and lithium-ion batteries.\n    10\t\n    11\t```\n    12\texport default () => (  <battery    name=\"BAT1\"    capacity=\"2500mAh\"  />)\n    13\t```\n    14\t\n    15\t![PCB Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pcb&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0utKMgvKlFISU1LLM0pUdDQVLC1U9DgUlCwSUosKUktqgQyFRTyEnNTbZWcHEMMlcD85MSCxOTMkkpbJSNTA4NcxwyQsL4dlyYAgqBGO08AAAA%3D)![Schematic Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=schematic&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0utKMgvKlFISU1LLM0pUdDQVLC1U9DgUlCwSUosKUktqgQyFRTyEnNTbZWcHEMMlcD85MSCxOTMkkpbJSNTA4NcxwyQsL4dlyYAgqBGO08AAAA%3D&simulation_experiment_id=simulation_experiment_0)![Pinout Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pinout&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0utKMgvKlFISU1LLM0pUdDQVLC1U9DgUlCwSUosKUktqgQyFRTyEnNTbZWcHEMMlcD85MSCxOTMkkpbJSNTA4NcxwyQsL4dlyYAgqBGO08AAAA%3D)![3D Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=3d&format=png&png_width=800&png_height=600&show_infinite_grid=true&background_color=%23ffffff&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0utKMgvKlFISU1LLM0pUdDQVLC1U9DgUlCwSUosKUktqgQyFRTyEnNTbZWcHEMMlcD85MSCxOTMkkpbJSNTA4NcxwyQsL4dlyYAgqBGO08AAAA%3D)\n    16\t\n    17\t## Pins[\u7ab6\u72a0(#pins \"Direct link to Pins\")\n    18\t\n    19\tA battery has the following pins and aliases:\n    20\t\n    21\tPin #\n    22\t\n    23\tAliases\n    24\t\n    25\tDescription\n    26\t\n    27\tpin1\n    28\t\n    29\tpos, positive, cathode\n    30\t\n    31\tThe positive terminal that provides current\n    32\t\n    33\tpin2\n    34\t\n    35\tneg, negative, anode\n    36\t\n    37\tThe negative terminal that completes the circuit\n    38\t\n    39\t## Specifications[\u7ab6\u72a0(#specifications \"Direct link to Specifications\")\n    40\t\n    41\tBatteries can be configured with these key properties:\n    42\t\n    43\t-   **capacity** - The energy storage capacity specified in mAh or Ah e.g. `\"2500mAh\"`, `\"1.2Ah\"`\n    44\t\n    45\t## Common Battery Types[\u7ab6\u72a0(#common-battery-types \"Direct link to Common Battery Types\")\n    46\t\n    47\tHere are some common battery types and their typical specifications:\n    48\t\n    49\tBattery Type\n    50\t\n    51\tVoltage\n    52\t\n    53\tTypical Capacity\n    54\t\n    55\tChemistry\n    56\t\n    57\tAA\n    58\t\n    59\t1.5V\n    60\t\n    61\t2000-3000mAh\n    62\t\n    63\tAlkaline\n    64\t\n    65\tAAA\n    66\t\n    67\t1.5V\n    68\t\n    69\t800-1200mAh\n    70\t\n    71\tAlkaline\n    72\t\n    73\t9V\n    74\t\n    75\t9V\n    76\t\n    77\t400-600mAh\n    78\t\n    79\tAlkaline\n    80\t\n    81\tCR2032\n    82\t\n    83\t3V\n    84\t\n    85\t200-250mAh\n    86\t\n    87\tLithium coin cell\n    88\t\n    89\t18650\n    90\t\n    91\t3.7V\n    92\t\n    93\t2500-3500mAh\n    94\t\n    95\tLithium-ion\n    96\t\n    97\t## Schematic Orientation[\u7ab6\u72a0(#schematic-orientation \"Direct link to Schematic Orientation\")\n    98\t\n    99\tBatteries can display their positive and negative terminals in different orientations. Use the `schOrientation` property to control the symbol orientation.\n   100\t\n   101\tValid orientation values are:\n   102\t\n   103\t-   `horizontal`\n   104\t-   `vertical`\n   105\t-   `pos_left`\n   106\t-   `pos_right`\n   107\t-   `pos_top`\n   108\t-   `pos_bottom`\n   109\t-   `neg_left`\n   110\t-   `neg_right`\n   111\t-   `neg_top`\n   112\t-   `neg_bottom`\n   113\t\n   114\t```\n   115\t<battery  name=\"BAT1\"  capacity=\"2500mAh\"  schOrientation=\"pos_left\"  schX={0}  schY={0}  connections={{ pos: \"net.VCC\", neg: \"net.GND\" }}/>\n   116\t```\n   117\t\n   118\t## Usage Examples[\u7ab6\u72a0(#usage-examples \"Direct link to Usage Examples\")\n   119\t\n   120\t### Basic Power Supply[\u7ab6\u72a0(#basic-power-supply \"Direct link to Basic Power Supply\")\n   121\t\n   122\t```\n   123\t<battery  name=\"BAT1\"  capacity=\"2000mAh\"/>\n   124\t```\n   125\t\n   126\t### High Capacity Battery[\u7ab6\u72a0(#high-capacity-battery \"Direct link to High Capacity Battery\")\n   127\t\n   128\t```\n   129\t<battery  name=\"BAT1\"  capacity=\"3000mAh\"/>\n   130\t```\n   131\t\n   132\t### Small Capacity Battery[\u7ab6\u72a0(#small-capacity-battery \"Direct link to Small Capacity Battery\")\n   133\t\n   134\t```\n   135\t<battery  name=\"BAT_RTC\"  capacity=\"220mAh\"/>\n   136\t```\n",
        "enable_truncation": true
      }
