  {
    "role": "tool",
    "content": [
      {
        "cache_prompt": false,
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/skills/tscircuit_operation_manual.md:\n     1\t# `tscircuit` Operational Guide\n     2\t\n     3\t## **Skill ID**\n     4\t\n     5\t`ANA-SKILL-TSCIRCUIT-OPERATION-GUIDE`\n     6\t\n     7\t## Circuit Assembly, Modules & Connectivity\n     8\t\n     9\t---\n    10\t\n    11\t## Overview\n    12\t\n    13\tThis guide describes **how to assemble circuits using `tscircuit`** by:\n    14\t\n    15\t* instantiating existing components\n    16\t* organizing them into modules\n    17\t* arranging schematic and PCB layouts\n    18\t* defining connectivity using nets and traces\n    19\t\n    20\tIt assumes that **all components referenced already exist** and are importable.\n    21\t\n    22\t---\n    23\t\n    24\t## 1. Circuit Structure\n    25\t\n    26\t### Root Container\n    27\t\n    28\tEvery circuit must be wrapped in a `<board />` element.\n    29\t\n    30\t```tsx\n    31\t<board width=\"100mm\" height=\"80mm\">\n    32\t  {/* circuit contents */}\n    33\t</board>\n    34\t```\n    35\t\n    36\t* `<board />` is the root of schematic and PCB generation\n    37\t* All components, nets, groups, and traces must be children of `<board />`\n    38\t\n    39\t---\n    40\t\n    41\t## 2. Using Existing Components\n    42\t\n    43\t### A. Built-in Primitives\n    44\t\n    45\t`tscircuit` provides globally available primitives that **do not require imports**.\n    46\t\n    47\tCommon examples:\n    48\t\n    49\t* `<resistor />`\n    50\t* `<capacitor />`\n    51\t* `<inductor />`\n    52\t* `<diode />`\n    53\t* `<led />`\n    54\t* `<jumper />`\n    55\t* `<pinheader />`\n    56\t\n    57\t#### Required Props for Passives\n    58\t\n    59\t| Element         | Required Props                     |\n    60\t| --------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n    61\t| `<resistor />`  | `name`, `resistance`, `footprint`  |\n    62\t| `<capacitor />` | `name`, `capacitance`, `footprint` |\n    63\t| `<inductor />`  | `name`, `inductance`, `footprint`  |\n    64\t| `<led />`       | `name`, `color`, `footprint`       |\n    65\t\n    66\tExample:\n    67\t\n    68\t```tsx\n    69\t<resistor\n    70\t  name=\"R1\"\n    71\t  resistance=\"10k\"\n    72\t  footprint=\"0603\"\n    73\t/>\n    74\t```\n    75\t\n    76\t---\n    77\t\n    78\t### B. Imported Components\n    79\t\n    80\tComponents defined elsewhere (e.g., ICs or reusable blocks) may be imported and instantiated.\n    81\t\n    82\t```tsx\n    83\timport { ControllerIC } from \"./lib/ControllerIC\"\n    84\t\n    85\t<ControllerIC name=\"U1\" />\n    86\t```\n    87\t\n    88\t* Imported components are treated as black boxes\n    89\t* Pin names must be used exactly as exposed by the component\n    90\t\n    91\t---\n    92\t\n    93\t## 3. Nets\n    94\t\n    95\t### Declaring Nets\n    96\t\n    97\tNamed nets are used for shared electrical nodes.\n    98\t\n    99\t```tsx\n   100\t<net name=\"VCC\" />\n   101\t<net name=\"GND\" />\n   102\t```\n   103\t\n   104\t* Nets should be declared near the top of the `<board />`\n   105\t* Nets may be referenced anywhere within the board\n   106\t\n   107\t---\n   108\t\n   109\t### Connecting to Nets\n   110\t\n   111\tPins may be connected directly to nets.\n   112\t\n   113\t```tsx\n   114\t<trace from=\".U1 > .VDD\" to=\"net.VCC\" />\n   115\t<trace from=\".U1 > .GND\" to=\"net.GND\" />\n   116\t```\n   117\t\n   118\t---\n   119\t\n   120\t## 4. Connectivity\n   121\t\n   122\t### A. Point-to-Point Traces\n   123\t\n   124\tUse `<trace />` to connect two pins.\n   125\t\n   126\t```tsx\n   127\t<trace from=\".U1 > .TX\" to=\".R1 > .pin1\" />\n   128\t```\n   129\t\n   130\t* `from` and `to` use CSS-like selectors\n   131\t* Pin identifiers depend on the component definition\n   132\t\n   133\t---\n   134\t\n   135\t### B. Mixed Connectivity\n   136\t\n   137\tBoth nets and direct traces may coexist.\n   138\t\n   139\t```tsx\n   140\t<trace from=\".C1 > .pin1\" to=\"net.VCC\" />\n   141\t<trace from=\".C1 > .pin2\" to=\"net.GND\" />\n   142\t```\n   143\t\n   144\t---\n   145\t\n   146\t## 5. Modular Organization with `<group />`\n   147\t\n   148\t### Purpose\n   149\t\n   150\t`<group />` is a container for organizing related components and traces.\n   151\t\n   152\tIt may be used to:\n   153\t\n   154\t* cluster functionally related elements\n   155\t* simplify layout\n   156\t* move multiple elements together\n   157\t\n   158\t---\n   159\t\n   160\t### Auto-Layout Support\n   161\t\n   162\t`<group />` supports automatic layout for schematic and PCB.\n   163\t\n   164\t#### Schematic Layout Props\n   165\t\n   166\t* `schFlex`\n   167\t* `schFlexDirection=\"row\" | \"column\"`\n   168\t* `schGap`\n   169\t\n   170\t#### PCB Layout Props\n   171\t\n   172\t* `pcbGrid`\n   173\t* `pcbGridCols`\n   174\t* `pcbGridGap`\n   175\t\n   176\t---\n   177\t\n   178\t### Example: Power Input Block\n   179\t\n   180\t```tsx\n   181\t<group\n   182\t  schFlex\n   183\t  schFlexDirection=\"row\"\n   184\t  schGap=\"2mm\"\n   185\t  pcbGrid\n   186\t  pcbGridCols={2}\n   187\t  pcbGridGap=\"1mm\"\n   188\t>\n   189\t  <resistor name=\"R_Fuse\" resistance=\"10\" footprint=\"0603\" />\n   190\t  <capacitor name=\"C_Bulk\" capacitance=\"100uF\" footprint=\"1206\" />\n   191\t\n   192\t  <trace from=\".R_Fuse > .pin2\" to=\".C_Bulk > .pos\" />\n   193\t</group>\n   194\t```\n   195\t\n   196\t---\n   197\t\n   198\t## 6. Placement\n   199\t\n   200\t### Manual Placement\n   201\t\n   202\tComponents or groups may be positioned explicitly.\n   203\t\n   204\t* Schematic: `schX`, `schY`\n   205\t* PCB: `pcbX`, `pcbY`\n   206\t\n   207\t```tsx\n   208\t<capacitor\n   209\t  name=\"C1\"\n   210\t  capacitance=\"100nF\"\n   211\t  footprint=\"0402\"\n   212\t  schX={10}\n   213\t  schY={5}\n   214\t  pcbX={12}\n   215\t  pcbY={8}\n   216\t/>\n   217\t```\n   218\t\n   219\t---\n   220\t\n   221\t### Placement Strategy\n   222\t\n   223\t* Manual coordinates are typically used at **top-level**\n   224\t* Auto-layout is preferred inside dense groups\n   225\t\n   226\t---\n   227\t\n   228\t## 7. Canonical Assembly Example\n   229\t\n   230\t```tsx\n   231\timport { ControllerIC } from \"./lib/ControllerIC\"\n   232\t\n   233\texport default () => {\n   234\t  return (\n   235\t    <board width=\"100mm\" height=\"80mm\">\n   236\t      <net name=\"VCC\" />\n   237\t      <net name=\"GND\" />\n   238\t\n   239\t      <ControllerIC name=\"U1\" />\n   240\t\n   241\t      <capacitor\n   242\t        name=\"C_Decouple\"\n   243\t        capacitance=\"100nF\"\n   244\t        footprint=\"0402\"\n   245\t      />\n   246\t\n   247\t      <trace from=\".U1 > .VDD\" to=\"net.VCC\" />\n   248\t      <trace from=\".U1 > .GND\" to=\"net.GND\" />\n   249\t      <trace from=\".C_Decouple > .pin1\" to=\"net.VCC\" />\n   250\t      <trace from=\".C_Decouple > .pin2\" to=\"net.GND\" />\n   251\t    </board>\n   252\t  )\n   253\t}\n   254\t```\n   255\t\n   256\t---\n   257\t\n   258\t## 8. Built-in Elements Reference\n   259\t\n   260\t| Element                           | Description               |\n   261\t| --------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n   262\t\n",
        "enable_truncation": true
      }
    ],
