    "role": "tool",
    "content": [
      {
        "cache_prompt": false,
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/skills/tsci_built_in_elements/jumper.md:\n     1\t# <jumper />\n     2\t\n     3\t## Overview\n     4\t\n     5\tA `<jumper />` represents a small multi-pin connector, commonly a male or female header using a `pinrow`-style footprint.\n     6\t\n     7\tYou can think of a jumper as a **flexible connector**, similar to a `<chip />`, that can be placed anywhere on the board.\n     8\t\n     9\t### Basic Example\n    10\t\n    11\t```tsx\n    12\texport default () => (\n    13\t  <board width=\"10mm\" height=\"10mm\">\n    14\t    <jumper name=\"J1\" footprint=\"pinrow4\" />\n    15\t  </board>\n    16\t)\n    17\t```\n    18\t\n    19\t### Previews\n    20\t\n    21\t![PCB Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pcb\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAAy3MQQqDMBBG4b2n%2BJmVrqzQpckBeouUjE1KkwnDiD1%2BU3H54OPxt4kaIm9h%2FxjGCc5jHID1KUEjjhwtOVpupRAS51eyq3xHnb330lhRQ2FHj4WwiVjTXLtruaocd8L8x%2Bt8Lv0w%2FQALjgfzdQAAAA%3D%3D)\n    22\t![Schematic Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=schematic\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAAy3MQQqDMBBG4b2n%2BJmVrqzQpckBeouUjE1KkwnDiD1%2BU3H54OPxt4kaIm9h%2FxjGCc5jHID1KUEjjhwtOVpupRAS51eyq3xHnb330lhRQ2FHj4WwiVjTXLtruaocd8L8x%2Bt8Lv0w%2FQALjgfzdQAAAA%3D%3D\\&simulation_experiment_id=simulation_experiment_0)\n    23\t![Pinout Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pinout\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAAy3MQQqDMBBG4b2n%2BJmVrqzQpckBeouUjE1KkwnDiD1%2BU3H54OPxt4kaIm9h%2FxjGCc5jHID1KUEjjhwtOVpupRAS51eyq3xHnb330lhRQ2FHj4WwiVjTXLtruaocd8L8x%2Bt8Lv0w%2FQALjgfzdQAAAA%3D%3D)\n    24\t![3D Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=3d\\&format=png\\&png_width=800\\&png_height=600\\&show_infinite_grid=true\\&background_color=%23ffffff\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAAy3MQQqDMBBG4b2n%2BJmVrqzQpckBeouUjE1KkwnDiD1%2BU3H54OPxt4kaIm9h%2FxjGCc5jHID1KUEjjhwtOVpupRAS51eyq3xHnb330lhRQ2FHj4WwiVjTXLtruaocd8L8x%2Bt8Lv0w%2FQALjgfzdQAAAA%3D%3D)\n    25\t\n    26\tThe example above is adapted from the\n    27\t[`jumper` core tests](https://github.com/tscircuit/core/blob/main/tests/components/normal-components/jumper.test.tsx).\n    28\t\n    29\t---\n    30\t\n    31\t## Properties\n    32\t\n    33\t`<jumper />` shares many common component properties such as `pcbX`, `pcbY`, and `footprint`.\n    34\t\n    35\tThe full TypeScript interface is defined in\n    36\t[`@tscircuit/props`](https://github.com/tscircuit/props/blob/main/lib/components/jumper.ts):\n    37\t\n    38\t```ts\n    39\texport interface JumperProps extends CommonComponentProps {\n    40\t  manufacturerPartNumber?: string\n    41\t  pinLabels?: Record<number | string, string | string[]>\n    42\t  schPinStyle?: SchematicPinStyle\n    43\t  schPinSpacing?: number | string\n    44\t  schWidth?: number | string\n    45\t  schHeight?: number | string\n    46\t  schDirection?: \"left\" | \"right\"\n    47\t  schPortArrangement?: SchematicPortArrangement\n    48\t\n    49\t  /** Number of pins on the jumper (2 or 3) */\n    50\t  pinCount?: 2 | 3\n    51\t\n    52\t  /**\n    53\t   * Groups of pins that are internally connected\n    54\t   * e.g., [[\"1\", \"2\"], [\"2\", \"3\"]]\n    55\t   */\n    56\t  internallyConnectedPins?: string[][]\n    57\t}\n    58\t```\n    59\t\n    60\tJumpers are commonly used with footprints such as:\n    61\t\n    62\t* `pinrow8`\n    63\t* `pinrow6_female_rows2`\n    64\t\n    65\tYou can also provide a custom `<footprint />`, just like with `<chip />`.\n    66\t\n    67\t---\n    68\t\n    69\t## Internally Connected Pins\n    70\t\n    71\tUse the `internallyConnectedPins` prop when the jumper has pins that should be **shorted (bridged)** together by default.\n    72\t\n    73\tPins may be referenced by their **labels**.\n    74\t\n    75\t### Example\n    76\t\n    77\t```tsx\n    78\texport default () => (\n    79\t  <board width=\"10mm\" height=\"10mm\">\n    80\t    <jumper\n    81\t      name=\"J2\"\n    82\t      footprint=\"pinrow3\"\n    83\t      pinCount={3}\n    84\t      pinLabels={{ 1: \"A\", 2: \"B\", 3: \"C\" }}\n    85\t      internallyConnectedPins={[\n    86\t        [\"A\", \"B\"],\n    87\t        [\"B\", \"C\"],\n    88\t      ]}\n    89\t    />\n    90\t  </board>\n    91\t)\n    92\t```\n    93\t\n    94\t### Previews\n    95\t\n    96\t![PCB Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pcb\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0WPQQ%2BCMAyF7%2F6KZidISBC4GSBRbsaDd8JhSJEZ2JY5gobw360T4un1te9rWnxpZSw02PKxt%2BD5kOXg7QDSWnHTwCQa22Us2g8Dgw7FvbOryylEscc4aDSuBpB8wIydY7b6VimrjZDEaCGNmpJtQrZQIw3mZPm3LrzG%2FpnNM0QHYEcWQEx6Ik1ICwbLFqadaCTv%2B3ehpMSbxeYqJKFl6TiCqgBKxxJYVT8w%2FF6dhu63fOd%2FANgCxjT%2BAAAA)\n    97\t![Schematic Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=schematic\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0WPQQ%2BCMAyF7%2F6KZidISBC4GSBRbsaDd8JhSJEZ2JY5gobw360T4un1te9rWnxpZSw02PKxt%2BD5kOXg7QDSWnHTwCQa22Us2g8Dgw7FvbOryylEscc4aDSuBpB8wIydY7b6VimrjZDEaCGNmpJtQrZQIw3mZPm3LrzG%2FpnNM0QHYEcWQEx6Ik1ICwbLFqadaCTv%2B3ehpMSbxeYqJKFl6TiCqgBKxxJYVT8w%2FF6dhu63fOd%2FANgCxjT%2BAAAA\\&simulation_experiment_id=simulation_experiment_0)\n    98\t![Pinout Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pinout\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0WPQQ%2BCMAyF7%2F6KZidISBC4GSBRbsaDd8JhSJEZ2JY5gobw360T4un1te9rWnxpZSw02PKxt%2BD5kOXg7QDSWnHTwCQa22Us2g8Dgw7FvbOryylEscc4aDSuBpB8wIydY7b6VimrjZDEaCGNmpJtQrZQIw3mZPm3LrzG%2FpnNM0QHYEcWQEx6Ik1ICwbLFqadaCTv%2B3ehpMSbxeYqJKFl6TiCqgBKxxJYVT8w%2FF6dhu63fOd%2FANgCxjT%2BAAAA)\n    99\t![3D Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=3d\\&format=png\\&png_width=800\\&png_height=600\\&show_infinite_grid=true\\&background_color=%23ffffff\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0WPQQ%2BCMAyF7%2F6KZidISBC4GSBRbsaDd8JhSJEZ2JY5gobw360T4un1te9rWnxpZSw02PKxt%2BD5kOXg7QDSWnHTwCQa22Us2g8Dgw7FvbOryylEscc4aDSuBpB8wIydY7b6VimrjZDEaCGNmpJtQrZQIw3mZPm3LrzG%2FpnNM0QHYEcWQEx6Ik1ICwbLFqadaCTv%2B3ehpMSbxeYqJKFl6TiCqgBKxxJYVT8w%2FF6dhu63fOd%2FANgCxjT%2BAAAA)\n   100\t\n   101\t---\n   102\t\n   103\t## Jumper-Specific Properties\n   104\t\n   105\t| Property                  | Type                                           | Description                                  |\n   106\t| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n   107\t| `pinCount`                | `2` | `3`                                      | Number of pins on the jumper                 |\n   108\t| `internallyConnectedPins` | `string[][]`                                   | Groups of pins that are internally connected |\n   109\t| `manufacturerPartNumber`  | `string`                                       | Manufacturer part number                     |\n   110\t| `pinLabels`               | `Record<number \\| string, string \\| string[]>` | Labels for individual pins or pin groups     |\n   111\t| `schPinStyle`             | `SchematicPinStyle`                            | Pin styling in the schematic                 |\n   112\t| `schPinSpacing`           | `number \\| string`                             | Spacing between schematic pins               |\n   113\t| `schWidth`                | `number \\| string`                             | Width of the schematic symbol                |\n   114\t| `schHeight`               | `number \\| string`                             | Height of the schematic symbol               |\n   115\t| `schDirection`            | `\"left\"` | `\"right\"`                           | Direction the jumper faces in the schematic  |\n   116\t| `schPortArrangement`      | `SchematicPortArrangement`                     | Arrangement of schematic ports               |\n   117\t\n   118\t\n",
        "enable_truncation": true
      }
    ],
