  {
    "role": "tool",
    "content": [
      {
        "cache_prompt": false,
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/skills/tsci_built_in_elements/switch.md:\n     1\t# <switch />\n     2\t\n     3\t## Overview\n     4\t\n     5\tA `<switch />` is a mechanical component used to **connect or disconnect** parts of a circuit.\n     6\t\n     7\t### Basic Example\n     8\t\n     9\t```tsx\n    10\texport default () => (\n    11\t  <switch name=\"SW1\" type=\"spst\" />\n    12\t)\n    13\t```\n    14\t\n    15\t### Previews\n    16\t\n    17\t![PCB Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pcb\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0utKMgvKlFISU1LLM0pUdDQVLC1U9DgUlCwKS7PLEnOUMhLzE21VQoON1RSKKksADKLC4pLlBT07bg0ARk6bBA8AAAA)\n    18\t![Schematic Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=schematic\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0utKMgvKlFISU1LLM0pUdDQVLC1U9DgUlCwKS7PLEnOUMhLzE21VQoON1RSKKksADKLC4pLlBT07bg0ARk6bBA8AAAA\\&simulation_experiment_id=simulation_experiment_0)\n    19\t![Pinout Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pinout\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0utKMgvKlFISU1LLM0pUdDQVLC1U9DgUlCwKS7PLEnOUMhLzE21VQoON1RSKKksADKLC4pLlBT07bg0ARk6bBA8AAAA)\n    20\t![3D Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=3d\\&format=png\\&png_width=800\\&png_height=600\\&show_infinite_grid=true\\&background_color=%23ffffff\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0utKMgvKlFISU1LLM0pUdDQVLC1U9DgUlCwKS7PLEnOUMhLzE21VQoON1RSKKksADKLC4pLlBT07bg0ARk6bBA8AAAA)\n    21\t\n    22\t---\n    23\t\n    24\t## Properties\n    25\t\n    26\t| Property           | Type                                      | Description                           |\n    27\t| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n    28\t| `type`             | `\"spst\"` | `\"spdt\"` | `\"dpst\"` | `\"dpdt\"` | Type of switch                        |\n    29\t| `isNormallyClosed` | `boolean`                                 | Whether the switch is normally closed |\n    30\t\n    31\t---\n    32\t\n    33\t## Types of Switches\n    34\t\n    35\t| Type   | Description                                                                        |\n    36\t| ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n    37\t| `spst` | **Single Pole Single Throw** \u2014 One input and one output                            |\n    38\t| `spdt` | **Single Pole Double Throw** \u2014 One input that can connect to either of two outputs |\n    39\t| `dpst` | **Double Pole Single Throw** \u2014 Two independent input/output pairs                  |\n    40\t| `dpdt` | **Double Pole Double Throw** \u2014 Two inputs, each selectable between two outputs     |\n    41\t\n    42\t### Example: Different Switch Types\n    43\t\n    44\t```tsx\n    45\texport default () => (\n    46\t  <group>\n    47\t    <switch name=\"SW1\" type=\"spst\" schX={-1} schY={-1} />\n    48\t    <switch name=\"SW2\" type=\"spdt\" schX={1} schY={-1} />\n    49\t    <switch name=\"SW3\" type=\"dpst\" schX={-1} schY={1} />\n    50\t    <switch name=\"SW4\" type=\"dpdt\" schX={1} schY={1} />\n    51\t  </group>\n    52\t)\n    53\t```\n    54\t\n    55\t### Previews\n    56\t\n    57\t![PCB Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pcb\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0utKMgvKlFISU1LLM0pUdDQVLC1U9DgUlCwSS%2FKLy2wA7KA7OLyzJLkDIW8xNxUW6XgcEMlhZLKAiCzuKC4REmhODkjwrZa17AWxIqEsPQJ6kyB6yRGozFMYwpWK3FrNEFoxGIjTJ%2BNPtS7mgCpFd%2FNEQEAAA%3D%3D)\n    58\t![Schematic Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=schematic\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0utKMgvKlFISU1LLM0pUdDQVLC1U9DgUlCwSS%2FKLy2wA7KA7OLyzJLkDIW8xNxUW6XgcEMlhZLKAiCzuKC4REmhODkjwrZa17AWxIqEsPQJ6kyB6yRGozFMYwpWK3FrNEFoxGIjTJ%2BNPtS7mgCpFd%2FNEQEAAA%3D%3D\\&simulation_experiment_id=simulation_experiment_0)\n    59\t![Pinout Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pinout\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0utKMgvKlFISU1LLM0pUdDQVLC1U9DgUlCwSS%2FKLy2wA7KA7OLyzJLkDIW8xNxUW6XgcEMlhZLKAiCzuKC4REmhODkjwrZa17AWxIqEsPQJ6kyB6yRGozFMYwpWK3FrNEFoxGIjTJ%2BNPtS7mgCpFd%2FNEQEAAA%3D%3D)\n    60\t![3D Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=3d\\&format=png\\&png_width=800\\&png_height=600\\&show_infinite_grid=true\\&background_color=%23ffffff\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA0utKMgvKlFISU1LLM0pUdDQVLC1U9DgUlCwSS%2FKLy2wA7KA7OLyzJLkDIW8xNxUW6XgcEMlhZLKAiCzuKC4REmhODkjwrZa17AWxIqEsPQJ6kyB6yRGozFMYwpWK3FrNEFoxGIjTJ%2BNPtS7mgCpFd%2FNEQEAAA%3D%3D)\n    61\t\n    62\t---\n    63\t\n    64\t## When to Use `<switch />` vs `<pushbutton />`\n    65\t\n    66\tWhenever possible, prefer using `<pushbutton />` or another **more specific switch component**.\n    67\t\n    68\t`<switch />` is a **generic, low-default** element intended for cases where no specialized switch abstraction fits your use case.\n    69\t\n",
        "enable_truncation": true
      }
    ],
