        "cache_prompt": false,
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/skills/tsci_built_in_elements/transistor.md:\n     1\t# <transistor />\n     2\t\n     3\t## Overview\n     4\t\n     5\tA `<transistor />` is a three-terminal semiconductor device used to **amplify** or **switch** electronic signals.\n     6\t\n     7\tTransistors are fundamental components in many circuits, including:\n     8\t\n     9\t* Amplifiers\n    10\t* Oscillators\n    11\t* Digital logic gates\n    12\t\n    13\t### Basic Example\n    14\t\n    15\t```tsx\n    16\texport default () => (\n    17\t  <transistor\n    18\t    name=\"Q1\"\n    19\t    type=\"npn\"\n    20\t    footprint=\"sot23\"\n    21\t  />\n    22\t)\n    23\t```\n    24\t\n    25\t### Previews\n    26\t\n    27\t![PCB Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pcb\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAAyXIMQ6AIAwAwJ1XNEwwGXUV%2FuATSISERNum1ER%2FL%2Bp4ly8mUdhySeeu4DyECM4ALCoJW21K0gWA6cjBrqP9pDd3IePPQqQsFTXYRjrN7w7R%2BAc8F92jXgAAAA%3D%3D)\n    28\t![Schematic Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=schematic\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAAyXIMQ6AIAwAwJ1XNEwwGXUV%2FuATSISERNum1ER%2FL%2Bp4ly8mUdhySeeu4DyECM4ALCoJW21K0gWA6cjBrqP9pDd3IePPQqQsFTXYRjrN7w7R%2BAc8F92jXgAAAA%3D%3D\\&simulation_experiment_id=simulation_experiment_0)\n    29\t![Pinout Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pinout\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAAyXIMQ6AIAwAwJ1XNEwwGXUV%2FuATSISERNum1ER%2FL%2Bp4ly8mUdhySeeu4DyECM4ALCoJW21K0gWA6cjBrqP9pDd3IePPQqQsFTXYRjrN7w7R%2BAc8F92jXgAAAA%3D%3D)\n    30\t![3D Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=3d\\&format=png\\&png_width=800\\&png_height=600\\&show_infinite_grid=true\\&background_color=%23ffffff\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAAyXIMQ6AIAwAwJ1XNEwwGXUV%2FuATSISERNum1ER%2FL%2Bp4ly8mUdhySeeu4DyECM4ALCoJW21K0gWA6cjBrqP9pDd3IePPQqQsFTXYRjrN7w7R%2BAc8F92jXgAAAA%3D%3D)\n    31\t\n    32\t---\n    33\t\n    34\t## Choosing the Right Transistor Element\n    35\t\n    36\tThere are multiple transistor types supported in `tscircuit`.\n    37\tWhenever possible, use the **most specific element** for clarity and better defaults:\n    38\t\n    39\t* [`<transistor />`](/elements/transistor) \u2014 Generic transistor\n    40\t* [`<mosfet />`](/elements/mosfet) \u2014 MOSFET transistor\n    41\t\n    42\t---\n    43\t\n    44\t## Properties\n    45\t\n    46\t| Property | Description                                                           | Example |\n    47\t| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------- |\n    48\t| `type`   | Type of transistor (`\"npn\"`, `\"pnp\"`, `\"mosfet\"`, `\"igbt\"`, `\"jfet\"`) | `\"npn\"` |\n    49\t\n    50\t\n",
        "enable_truncation": true
      }
    ],
