        "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/skills/tsci_built_in_elements/testpoint.md:\n     1\t# <testpoint />\n     2\t\n     3\t## Overview\n     4\t\n     5\tA `<testpoint />` is a designated location on a PCB that provides easy access for **testing, debugging, and measuring electrical signals**.\n     6\t\n     7\tTest points are essential during:\n     8\t\n     9\t* Circuit bring-up and debugging\n    10\t* Manufacturing test and validation\n    11\t* Field diagnostics and troubleshooting\n    12\t\n    13\tThey can be implemented as:\n    14\t\n    15\t* **Surface-mount pads**\n    16\t* **Through-hole connections**\n    17\t\n    18\tThe choice depends on probe type, board density, and testing frequency.\n    19\t\n    20\tWhen designing test points, consider probe compatibility, spacing, and labeling.\n    21\t\n    22\t### Basic Example\n    23\t\n    24\t```tsx\n    25\texport default () => (\n    26\t  <testpoint\n    27\t    name=\"TP1\"\n    28\t    footprintVariant=\"pad\"\n    29\t    padShape=\"circle\"\n    30\t    padDiameter=\"1mm\"\n    31\t  />\n    32\t)\n    33\t```\n    34\t\n    35\t### Previews\n    36\t\n    37\t![PCB Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pcb\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAAz2MMQqFQAxEe08RttLqY%2F%2FXygMIin3QiAvubogRPL5RwW7mvWHo5CwKMy14bAplBb6BsgD4K%2B3KOSS1ApAwkndDV7unLjkri8kRJWBS7xjnV1noV2RbT0GmjT7aBvtQEu%2FqGG%2F6a4rqAuzaqKOAAAAA)\n    38\t![Schematic Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=schematic\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAAz2MMQqFQAxEe08RttLqY%2F%2FXygMIin3QiAvubogRPL5RwW7mvWHo5CwKMy14bAplBb6BsgD4K%2B3KOSS1ApAwkndDV7unLjkri8kRJWBS7xjnV1noV2RbT0GmjT7aBvtQEu%2FqGG%2F6a4rqAuzaqKOAAAAA\\&simulation_experiment_id=simulation_experiment_0)\n    39\t![Pinout Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pinout\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAAz2MMQqFQAxEe08RttLqY%2F%2FXygMIin3QiAvubogRPL5RwW7mvWHo5CwKMy14bAplBb6BsgD4K%2B3KOSS1ApAwkndDV7unLjkri8kRJWBS7xjnV1noV2RbT0GmjT7aBvtQEu%2FqGG%2F6a4rqAuzaqKOAAAAA)\n    40\t![3D Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=3d\\&format=png\\&png_width=800\\&png_height=600\\&show_infinite_grid=true\\&background_color=%23ffffff\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAAz2MMQqFQAxEe08RttLqY%2F%2FXygMIin3QiAvubogRPL5RwW7mvWHo5CwKMy14bAplBb6BsgD4K%2B3KOSS1ApAwkndDV7unLjkri8kRJWBS7xjnV1noV2RbT0GmjT7aBvtQEu%2FqGG%2F6a4rqAuzaqKOAAAAA)\n    41\t\n    42\t---\n    43\t\n    44\t## Pins\n    45\t\n    46\tA test point has a **single electrical connection**.\n    47\t\n    48\t| Pin    | Aliases      | Description           |\n    49\t| ------ | ------------ | --------------------- |\n    50\t| `pin1` | `tp`, `test` | Test point connection |\n    51\t\n    52\t---\n    53\t\n    54\t## Properties\n    55\t\n    56\t| Property           | Type                       | Required | Description                                       | Example                   |\n    57\t| ------------------ | -------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n    58\t| `footprintVariant` | `\"pad\"` | `\"through_hole\"` | No       | Type of test point implementation                 | `\"pad\"`, `\"through_hole\"` |\n    59\t| `padShape`         | `\"rect\"` | `\"circle\"`      | No       | Shape of the test point pad (default: `\"circle\"`) | `\"circle\"`, `\"rect\"`      |\n    60\t| `padDiameter`      | `string \\| number`         | No       | Diameter of circular pads                         | `\"1mm\"`, `0.5`            |\n    61\t| `holeDiameter`     | `string \\| number`         | No       | Diameter of hole for through-hole test points     | `\"0.8mm\"`, `0.3`          |\n    62\t| `width`            | `string \\| number`         | No       | Width of rectangular pads                         | `\"2mm\"`, `1.5`            |\n    63\t| `height`           | `string \\| number`         | No       | Height of rectangular pads                        | `\"1mm\"`, `0.8`            |\n    64\t| `layer`            | `\"top\"` | `\"bottom\"`       | No       | PCB layer placement (default: `\"top\"`)            | `\"bottom\"`                |\n    65\t\n    66\t---\n    67\t\n    68\t## Footprint Variants\n    69\t\n    70\t### Surface-Mount Pad (`footprintVariant=\"pad\"`)\n    71\t\n    72\tSurface-mount test points are exposed copper pads on the PCB surface.\n    73\t\n    74\t**Advantages**\n    75\t\n    76\t* Minimal board space\n    77\t* No drilling required\n    78\t* Suitable for automated testing\n    79\t\n    80\t**Use Cases**\n    81\t\n    82\t* High-density layouts\n    83\t* Automated test equipment (ATE)\n    84\t* Quick voltage or signal checks\n    85\t\n    86\t---\n    87\t\n    88\t### Through-Hole (`footprintVariant=\"through_hole\"`)\n    89\t\n    90\tThrough-hole test points include a drilled hole for secure probe attachment.\n    91\t\n    92\t**Advantages**\n    93\t\n    94\t* Better probe retention\n    95\t* More reliable repeated connections\n    96\t* Ideal for manual probing\n    97\t\n    98\t**Use Cases**\n    99\t\n   100\t* Prototyping\n   101\t* Manual debugging\n   102\t* Test fixtures and jigs\n   103\t\n   104\t---\n   105\t\n   106\t## Pad Shapes\n   107\t\n   108\t### Circle (`padShape=\"circle\"`)\n   109\t\n   110\tCircular pads are the most common and allow probing from any angle.\n   111\t\n   112\t```tsx\n   113\t<testpoint\n   114\t  name=\"TP1\"\n   115\t  footprintVariant=\"pad\"\n   116\t  padShape=\"circle\"\n   117\t  padDiameter=\"1mm\"\n   118\t/>\n   119\t```\n   120\t\n   121\t---\n   122\t\n   123\t### Rectangle (`padShape=\"rect\"`)\n   124\t\n   125\tRectangular pads provide additional contact area in tight layouts.\n   126\t\n   127\t```tsx\n   128\t<testpoint\n   129\t  name=\"TP2\"\n   130\t  footprintVariant=\"pad\"\n   131\t  padShape=\"rect\"\n   132\t  width=\"1.5mm\"\n   133\t  height=\"0.8mm\"\n   134\t/>\n   135\t```\n   136\t\n   137\t---\n   138\t\n   139\t## Sizing Guidelines\n   140\t\n   141\t### Pad Diameter / Size\n   142\t\n   143\t* **Small**: 0.5 mm \u2013 0.8 mm (high-density boards)\n   144\t* **Medium**: 1 mm \u2013 1.5 mm (general-purpose testing)\n   145\t* **Large**: 2 mm+ (manual probing)\n   146\t\n   147\t### Hole Diameter (Through-Hole)\n   148\t\n   149\t* **Standard**: 0.8 mm \u2013 1 mm\n   150\t* **Large probes**: 1.2 mm \u2013 1.5 mm\n   151\t\n   152\t---\n   153\t\n   154\t## Usage Examples\n   155\t\n   156\t### Basic Voltage Test Point\n   157\t\n   158\t```tsx\n   159\t<testpoint name=\"VCC_TP\" />\n   160\t```\n   161\t\n   162\t### Bottom-Layer Test Point\n   163\t\n   164\t```tsx\n   165\t<testpoint name=\"GND_TP\" layer=\"bottom\" />\n   166\t```\n   167\t\n   168\t### Custom Circular Pad\n   169\t\n   170\t```tsx\n   171\t<testpoint\n   172\t  name=\"SIG_TP\"\n   173\t  footprintVariant=\"pad\"\n   174\t  padShape=\"circle\"\n   175\t  padDiameter=\"1.2mm\"\n   176\t/>\n   177\t```\n   178\t\n   179\t### Through-Hole Test Point\n   180\t\n   181\t```tsx\n   182\t<testpoint\n   183\t  name=\"DEBUG_TP\"\n   184\t  footprintVariant=\"through_hole\"\n   185\t  holeDiameter=\"1mm\"\n   186\t  padDiameter=\"2mm\"\n   187\t/>\n   188\t```\n   189\t\n   190\t### Rectangular Test Point\n   191\t\n   192\t```tsx\n   193\t<testpoint\n   194\t  name=\"COMPACT_TP\"\n   195\t  footprintVariant=\"pad\"\n   196\t  padShape=\"rect\"\n   197\t  width=\"1.5mm\"\n   198\t  height=\"0.8mm\"\n   199\t/>\n   200\t```\n   201\t\n   202\t---\n   203\t\n   204\t## Testing Considerations\n   205\t\n   206\t* **Probe compatibility** \u2014 Match pad size to probe tips\n   207\t* **Spacing** \u2014 Leave room for probe access\n   208\t* **Labeling** \u2014 Use clear, descriptive names\n   209\t* **Documentation** \u2014 Include test points in schematics, assembly drawings, and test procedures\n   210\t\n   211\t\n",
        "enable_truncation": true
      }
    ],
