  {
    "role": "tool",
    "content": [
      {
        "cache_prompt": false,
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/skills/tsci_built_in_elements/via.md:\n     1\t# <via />\n     2\t\n     3\t## Overview\n     4\t\n     5\tA `<via />` is a **plated hole** that electrically connects different layers of a PCB.\n     6\tVias are commonly used for:\n     7\t\n     8\t* Routing traces between layers\n     9\t* Thermal relief and heat spreading\n    10\t\n    11\tVias **do not have a schematic representation**.\n    12\t\n    13\tIn most designs, you **do not need to manually place vias**\u2014they are typically inserted automatically by the\n    14\t[autorouter](/elements/board#setting-the-autorouter).\n    15\t\n    16\t### Basic Example\n    17\t\n    18\t```tsx\n    19\texport default () => (\n    20\t  <board width={5} height={5}>\n    21\t    <via\n    22\t      fromLayer=\"top\"\n    23\t      toLayer=\"bottom\"\n    24\t      outerDiameter=\"0.8mm\"\n    25\t      holeDiameter=\"0.4mm\"\n    26\t      pcbX={0}\n    27\t      pcbY={0}\n    28\t    />\n    29\t  </board>\n    30\t)\n    31\t```\n    32\t\n    33\t### Previews\n    34\t\n    35\t![PCB Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pcb\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA02OOw6DMBBEe06xooImUCRSCuwqZQ6QlHa8xJaw1rKWfIS4ewwiQLUz720x%2BAkUGQy2qu8YihKEhCIDaDSpaODtDFsxnEaw6J6WpyiTTg8vp%2BYA0EbyV%2FXFKHKmkC%2BUaWGamMn%2FMfWM8eKUx3RFXh%2FOfnWWOtyr46bCQ9%2FEUI9bva%2B1mhY11bxYZuUPeWMYv9QAAAA%3D)\n    36\t![Schematic Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=schematic\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA02OOw6DMBBEe06xooImUCRSCuwqZQ6QlHa8xJaw1rKWfIS4ewwiQLUz720x%2BAkUGQy2qu8YihKEhCIDaDSpaODtDFsxnEaw6J6WpyiTTg8vp%2BYA0EbyV%2FXFKHKmkC%2BUaWGamMn%2FMfWM8eKUx3RFXh%2FOfnWWOtyr46bCQ9%2FEUI9bva%2B1mhY11bxYZuUPeWMYv9QAAAA%3D\\&simulation_experiment_id=simulation_experiment_0)\n    37\t![Pinout Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=pinout\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA02OOw6DMBBEe06xooImUCRSCuwqZQ6QlHa8xJaw1rKWfIS4ewwiQLUz720x%2BAkUGQy2qu8YihKEhCIDaDSpaODtDFsxnEaw6J6WpyiTTg8vp%2BYA0EbyV%2FXFKHKmkC%2BUaWGamMn%2FMfWM8eKUx3RFXh%2FOfnWWOtyr46bCQ9%2FEUI9bva%2B1mhY11bxYZuUPeWMYv9QAAAA%3D)\n    38\t![3D Circuit Preview](https://svg.tscircuit.com/?svg_type=3d\\&format=png\\&png_width=800\\&png_height=600\\&show_infinite_grid=true\\&background_color=%23ffffff\\&code=H4sIAJsBqGcAA02OOw6DMBBEe06xooImUCRSCuwqZQ6QlHa8xJaw1rKWfIS4ewwiQLUz720x%2BAkUGQy2qu8YihKEhCIDaDSpaODtDFsxnEaw6J6WpyiTTg8vp%2BYA0EbyV%2FXFKHKmkC%2BUaWGamMn%2FMfWM8eKUx3RFXh%2FOfnWWOtyr46bCQ9%2FEUI9bva%2B1mhY11bxYZuUPeWMYv9QAAAA%3D)\n    39\t\n    40\t---\n    41\t\n    42\t## Properties\n    43\t\n    44\t| Property          | Type               | Default    | Description                                                                                             |\n    45\t| ----------------- | ------------------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n    46\t| `fromLayer`       | `string`           | `\"top\"`    | Starting PCB layer for the via                                                                          |\n    47\t| `toLayer`         | `string`           | `\"bottom\"` | Ending PCB layer for the via                                                                            |\n    48\t| `holeDiameter`    | `number \\| string` | `\"0.4mm\"`  | Diameter of the plated hole                                                                             |\n    49\t| `outerDiameter`   | `number \\| string` | `\"0.8mm\"`  | Outer diameter of the copper annular ring                                                               |\n    50\t| `pcbX`            | `number`           | `0`        | X position of the via on the PCB                                                                        |\n    51\t| `pcbY`            | `number`           | `0`        | Y position of the via on the PCB                                                                        |\n    52\t| `netIsAssignable` | `boolean`          | `false`    | Marks the via as prefabricated so autorouters (e.g. `laser_prefab`) may claim it for any compatible net |\n    53\t\n    54\tFor workflows using prefabricated vias and laser routing, see the\n    55\t[Biscuit Board Laser Ablation guide](/guides/tscircuit-essentials/biscuit-board-laser-ablation).\n    56\t\n    57\t\n",
        "enable_truncation": true
      }
    ],
